            <ArticleTitle>Coronary heart disease in women: evaluation and management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>955-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary heart disease should not be considered a male dominated disease. The incidence of clinical CHD lags by several years in women, but it remains a leading cause of death and disability in the adult female. Risk factors for the development of coronary atherosclerosis are essentially the same for both sexes. Management strategies are usually similar regardless of gender.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
